        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>1. Analyze Config (CVar Analyzer)</h2>
          <span class="author-tag">CVarAnalyzer.kt</span>
        </div>

        <p class="lead-text">
          The <strong>Analyze Config</strong> button invokes <code>CVarAnalyzer.kt</code> to cross-check active on-device INI CVars against the execution stream of decrypted <code>Client.log</code>. It resolves the <strong>latest instance</strong> near log end to determine whether your commands applied, failed, or were deleted by the game engine.
        </p>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>Config Analysis Report (<code>ConfigAnalysisDialog.kt</code>)</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Summary KPIs:</strong> Total CVars, Applied %, Failed count, Deleted/Ignored count &amp; %.</li>
            <li><strong>Collapsible Smart Insights Panel:</strong> Analyzes potential engine bottlenecks and provides actionable recommendations.</li>
            <li><strong>Combined Single Horizontal Filter Bar:</strong> Features a tap-to-cycle <strong>CVar Filter</strong> (<code>All</code> → <code>Applied</code> → <code>Failed</code> → <code>Deleted</code>) combined with a <strong>File Filter</strong> (<code>All Files</code> → <code>Engine.ini</code> → <code>DeviceProfiles.ini</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Copy &amp; Save Scope Dialogs:</strong> Selectively copy or export either the Full Report or Filtered CVar Names Only.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h4>Frozen Left Column Table Format</h4>
