      <section id="enable-csharp" class="doc-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Force Enable C# Environment Scripting</h2>
          <span class="author-tag">Editor Tab &gt; Misc Patch</span>
        </div>
        
        <p class="lead-text">
          WuWa Mobile Config Patcher includes support for checking, forcing, and verifying the experimental C# (C-Sharp) runtime environment for Wuthering Waves on Android.
        </p>

        <hr>

        <h3>Visual Reference & Toggle UI</h3>
        <div class="screenshot-grid" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 580px;">
          <div class="screenshot-card">
            <img src="../images/csharp.jpg" alt="Enable C# Environment Settings UI" class="screenshot-img">
            <div class="screenshot-caption">C# Environment Toggle</div>
            <div class="screenshot-subtext">Toggle C# runtime scripting pipeline and verify device RAM compatibility.</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr>

        <h3>What is the C# Environment?</h3>
        <p>
          Kuro Games developed an updated C# scripting pipeline for Wuthering Waves. Pushing the engine command-line flag <code>-ForceEnableCSharpEnvironment</code> forces the game engine to utilize this alternate scripting pipeline. When paired with compatible Vulkan graphics drivers, it can offer substantial frame pacing improvements, reduced CPU overhead, and smoother asset streaming on supported mobile hardware.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-warning">
          <div class="alert-title">⚠️ HARDWARE & RAM RECOMMENDATIONS</div>
          <strong>Recommended Physical RAM:</strong> 8 GB or higher. Devices with under 8 GB RAM may experience severe memory pressure or force-closing during intensive combat scenes or map loading.
        </div>

        <hr>

        <h3>How to Enable via Config Patcher</h3>
        <ol class="step-list">
          <li>Open <strong>WuWa Config Patcher</strong>.</li>
          <li>Navigate to <strong>Editor Tab &gt; Misc Patch Subtab</strong>.</li>
          <li>Check <code>-ForceEnableCSharpEnvironment</code> (and optionally <code>-SkipSplash</code>).</li>
          <li>Tap <strong>Patch</strong>. This pushes the command flag directly into <code>.../files/UE4Game/Client/UE4CommandLine.txt</code>.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="alert alert-tip">
          <div class="alert-title">💡 VERIFICATION METHODS</div>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>In-Game Client Version Asterisk (*):</strong> Launch Wuthering Waves. Inspect the version string on the top-right or bottom-left of the splash screen. An <strong>asterisk (*)</strong> at the end of the version string confirms C# is active!</li>
            <li><strong>Log Verification:</strong> Go to <strong>Utilities &gt; Decrypted Log Explorer</strong> and search for <code>Sharphereal</code>. If present with initialization logs, C# is active.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <hr>

        <h3>Reverting or Disabling</h3>
        <p>
          If your device experiences instability with C# enabled, simply reopen <strong>Misc Patch</strong> and uncheck <code>-ForceEnableCSharpEnvironment</code>, or tap <strong>Revert to Vanilla</strong> in Utilities to restore default engine launch scripts.
        </p>

      </section>
