          <h2>Manual Mode Guide (Old School File Managers)</h2>
          <span class="author-tag">Fallback Workflow for Android 11 to 13</span>
        </div>

        <p class="lead-text">
          If you are unable to set up Shizuku, Wireless Debugging, or Root access, you can manually export presets from the patcher and paste them into the game's scoped storage folder using specialized file managers or USB PC transfers.
        </p>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>Manual Patching Instructions</h4>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Install a Scoped Storage-compatible file manager such as <strong>FV File Explorer</strong>, <strong>ZArchiver</strong>, or <strong>MT Manager</strong>.</li>
            <li>In WuWa Config Patcher, go to <strong>Utilities &gt; Export &amp; Sharing &gt; Share Patch</strong> to export your desired configuration archive.</li>
            <li>Extract the <code>Engine.ini</code>, <code>DeviceProfiles.ini</code>, and <code>Scalability.ini</code> files.</li>
            <li>Using your file explorer, copy the files and navigate to:
              <br><code style="display: block; margin: 8px 0; word-break: break-all;">/storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.kurogame.wutheringwaves.global/files/UE4Game/Client/Client/Saved/Config/Android/</code>
            </li>
            <li>Paste and overwrite the existing files.</li>
            <li>Launch Wuthering Waves.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-important">
          <div class="alert-title">ANDROID 14 / 15 PERMISSION RESTRICTIONS</div>
          On newer Android versions (Android 14 and 15+), Google has blocked third-party file managers without elevated Shizuku or Root access from reaching <code>/Android/data/</code>. In this scenario, setting up Shizuku or Root for WuWa Config Patcher is strictly required.
        </div>
      </section>

    </main>
