          <li><a href="bug-reporting.html" class="nav-link">Support & Activity Logger</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <main class="content-area">
      
      <section class="doc-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Elevated Access Backends Hierarchy</h2>
          <span class="author-tag">Target SDK 36 • Android 11 to 15+</span>
        </div>

        <p class="lead-text">
          On Android 11+, Google restricts direct access to <code>/Android/data/</code> via Scoped Storage (Storage Access Framework). WuWa Config Patcher bypasses these limitations using elevated IPC backends so you can patch files without needing a PC or a rooted device.
        </p>

        <div class="features-grid">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="badge-backend badge-root">ROOT</span>
            <h4 style="margin-top: 10px;">1. ROOT (Native SU)</h4>
            <p>Managed via topjohnwu <code>libsu</code> Core (<code>v6.0.0</code>). Direct elevated root shell execution (<code>su -c id</code>).</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="badge-backend badge-shizuku">SHIZUKU</span>
            <h4 style="margin-top: 10px;">2. SHIZUKU (Wireless ADB)</h4>
            <p>Managed via <code>ShizukuManager.kt</code> (`rikka.shizuku.api`). Wireless ADB IPC execution requiring zero root.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="badge-backend badge-axmanager">AXMANAGER</span>
            <h4 style="margin-top: 10px;">3. AXMANAGER</h4>
            <p>Managed via <code>AxManagerManager.kt</code>. Axeron community provider helper integration.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="badge-backend badge-unauthorized">SHIZUKU_UNAUTHORIZED</span>
            <h4 style="margin-top: 10px;">4. SHIZUKU UNAUTHORIZED</h4>
            <p>Shizuku service binder detected running on device, but app permission prompt is pending approval.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-card">
            <span class="badge-backend badge-none">NONE</span>
            <h4 style="margin-top: 10px;">5. NONE</h4>
            <p>No elevated backend available. Prompts Shizuku setup wizard or falls back to manual file export.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Standard Guide: Setting up Shizuku (Wireless Debugging)</h2>
          <span class="author-tag">End-User Setup (No Root Required)</span>
        </div>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>Step-by-Step Wireless Debugging Pairing</h4>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Download and install <strong>Shizuku</strong> from Google Play or official GitHub releases.</li>
            <li>Connect your device to <strong>Wi-Fi</strong> (or turn on Portable Wi-Fi Hotspot on your phone).</li>
            <li>Go to <strong>Settings &gt; Developer Options</strong> on your phone.
              <ul>
                <li>Enable <strong>Developer Options</strong> (tap <em>Build Number</em> 7 times in <em>About Phone</em>).</li>
                <li>Enable <strong>USB Debugging</strong> and <strong>Wireless Debugging</strong>.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Open Shizuku, tap <strong>Pairing</strong> &gt; <strong>Developer Options</strong>, then tap <strong>Pair device with pairing code</strong>.</li>
            <li>Enter the 6-digit code in the Shizuku notification prompt.</li>
            <li>Return to Shizuku and tap <strong>Start</strong> until status shows <em>"Shizuku is running"</em>.</li>
            <li>Open <strong>WuWa Config Patcher</strong> and grant Shizuku permission when prompted.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-important">
          <div class="alert-title">XIAOMI / HYPEROS / MIUI USERS</div>
          You must enable <strong>"USB Debugging (Security Settings)"</strong> inside Developer Options. This requires a signed-in Mi Account and allows Shizuku to grant file system write permissions.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Technical Deep-Dive: Elevation Architecture</h2>
          <span class="author-tag">ShizukuManager.kt & libsu</span>
        </div>

        <div class="code-block">
          <div class="code-header">Backend Verification Logic (ShizukuManager.kt)</div>
          <pre><code>// 1. Shizuku Binder IPC Check (rikka.shizuku.api)
val isShizukuAvailable = Shizuku.pingBinder()
if (isShizukuAvailable && Shizuku.checkSelfPermission() == PackageManager.PERMISSION_GRANTED) {
    activeBackend = AccessBackend.SHIZUKU // Green Badge (#47D764)
}

// 2. Direct Root Shell Fallback (libsu Core v6.0.0)
else if (Shell.cmd("id").exec().isSuccess) {
    activeBackend = AccessBackend.ROOT // Red Badge (#E35D6A)
}

// 3. Axeron Provider Detection (AxManagerManager.kt)
else if (AxManager.isAvailable()) {
    activeBackend = AccessBackend.AXMANAGER // Blue Badge (#2AA37D)
}

// 4. Unauthorized Pending Status
else if (isShizukuAvailable) {
    activeBackend = AccessBackend.SHIZUKU_UNAUTHORIZED // Orange Badge (#F7C948)
}

// 5. Fallback
else {
    activeBackend = AccessBackend.NONE // Gray Badge (#A8B4AF)
}</code></pre>
        </div>

        <p class="lead-text">
          When 1-Click Patch is triggered, the patcher uses Shizuku's elevated shell service to write directly to <code>/storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.kurogame.wutheringwaves.global/files/UE4Game/Client/Client/Saved/Config/Android/</code> without touching standard Android SAF document trees.
        </p>
      </section>

