        <div class="section-header">
          <h2>Troubleshooting & Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <span class="author-tag">v1.5.0 Support Reference</span>
        </div>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>1. Shizuku is Running, but App Shows "NONE" or Requests Access</h4>
          <p>If your Elevated Access Status shows "NONE" despite Shizuku running in the background:</p>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Go to the <strong>Settings</strong> tab and check the Elevated Access Status card.</li>
            <li>Tap the refresh button next to the Shizuku setup wizard.</li>
            <li>If it fails, open the Shizuku app, revoke permissions for WuWa Config Patcher, and force stop the patcher. Reopen the patcher to trigger the prompt again via <code>rikka.shizuku.api</code>.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>2. Game Stuttering or Crashing After Patching</h4>
          <p>Not all mobile devices handle extreme visual presets well. To safely reset your game graphics to Kuro Games' defaults:</p>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Navigate to the <strong>Utilities</strong> tab $\rightarrow$ <strong>Common Subtab</strong>.</li>
            <li>Tap the primary red <strong>Revert to Vanilla</strong> button.</li>
            <li>Confirm the prompt. This automatically executes a safe deletion of <code>Engine.ini</code>, <code>DeviceProfiles.ini</code>, and <code>Scalability.ini</code>.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>3. What do the Access Badges Mean?</h4>
          <ul class="step-list">
            <li><span class="badge-backend badge-root">ROOT</span> — Red badge (#E35D6A): Direct elevated <code>libsu</code> shell execution.</li>
            <li><span class="badge-backend badge-shizuku">SHIZUKU</span> — Green badge (#47D764): Primary wireless debugging ADB backend.</li>
            <li><span class="badge-backend badge-axmanager">AXMANAGER</span> — Blue badge (#2AA37D): Axeron community provider helper.</li>
            <li><span class="badge-backend badge-unauthorized">SHIZUKU_UNAUTHORIZED</span> — Orange badge (#F7C948): Shizuku binder running, permission pending.</li>
            <li><span class="badge-backend badge-none">NONE</span> — Gray badge (#A8B4AF): No elevated backend available.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>4. Editor Saves are Flagged in Vibrant Red (#FF2222)</h4>
          <p>The Config Editor enforces strict CVar Section Guards via <code>CVarSectionGuard.kt</code>. Misplaced lines or <code>Engine.ini</code> <code>CVars=</code> prefixes are painted bold <strong class="guard-red-highlight">Vibrant Red</strong>.</p>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>When you tap <strong>Save</strong>, select <strong>Auto-Fix Sections</strong> in the warning prompt.</li>
            <li>The app will automatically route your CVars to canonical section headers (e.g. <code>s.</code> commands to <code>[/Script/Engine.StreamingSettings]</code>) and strip invalid <code>CVars=</code> prefixes.</li>
            <li>Note: <code>[Core.Paths]</code>, <code>[Core.System]</code>, and <code>[/Script/Engine.RendererOverrideSettings]</code> are whitelisted and never altered.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>5. Internal Device Storage Full from Game Logs</h4>
          <p>Wuthering Waves can generate massive log files over time. To clean them:</p>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Go to <strong>Utilities</strong> $\rightarrow$ <strong>Common Subtab</strong> $\rightarrow$ <strong>Log Tools</strong>.</li>
            <li>Tap <strong>Delete Logs</strong> to execute an elevated <code>rm -rf</code> on the <code>.../Saved/Logs/</code> directory safely.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="method-card">
          <h4>6. Shader Compilation Crashes or Graphical Artifacts</h4>
          <p>If you experience rendering artifacts or crashes during shader compilation after game updates:</p>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Go to <strong>Settings Tab &gt; Danger Zone</strong>.</li>
            <li>Tap <strong>Delete Shaders</strong>. This opens <code>DeleteShadersDialog.kt</code>.</li>
            <li>Select and delete Vulkan (<code>VulkanProgramBinaryCache</code>) or OpenGL (<code>ProgramBinaryCache</code>) shader caches to force a clean shader rebuild upon next launch.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
